      {
        "id": 4304638418,
        "review_id": 5560243413,
        "path": "scripts/agent-control/lib/merge-grant.mjs",
        "line": 233,
        "created_at": "2026-10-17T21:44:23Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-17T21:44:23Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/SaCH-PRO/KEYFLOWOS/pull/181#discussion_r4304638418",
        "body": "[P1] Require an effect-valid HOLD_CLEAR before clearing the hold. AUTHORITY-profile validity is weaker than readEffect validity: HOLD_SET → RESUME/NO_STATE_CHANGE → exact grant currently returns granted:true, and the actual mocked --merge CLI makes one SHA-pinned synthetic PUT after two snapshots, even though readEffect rejects the RESUME as CONTROL_EFFECT_TYPE_MISMATCH. Missing/unknown effects and invalid safety/health values reproduce the same pure-predicate defect. Preserve the active hold unless a valid target HOLD_CLEAR releases it, and add a live distinguishing control."
      },
      {
        "id": 4304638419,
        "review_id": 5560243413,
        "path": "scripts/agent-control/tests/merge-cli.spec.mjs",
        "line": 80,
        "created_at": "2026-10-17T21:44:23Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-17T21:44:23Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/SaCH-PRO/KEYFLOWOS/pull/181#discussion_r4304638419",
        "body": "[P2] Move the large pagination fixture out of a single environment variable. The two-snapshot scenario serializes to about 174 KB here; on Node 20/Linux spawnSync fails with E2BIG before starting the CLI, so the pagination test gets status null and never reads #80. The same null-status assertion fails in current artifact Ubuntu Worker Proof and Autopilot self-test. Use a bounded file/stream fixture transport and expose child.error while preserving multi-page grant/revocation and two-snapshot coverage."
      }
    ],
